}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}-\\frac{9}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\frac{9}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{9}{8}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{8}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339930 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339931 13194139535253 true] [17592186339930 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339932 13194139535253 true] [17592186339930 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535253 true] [17592186339930 1041 "field-1" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339930 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339931 13194139535253 true] [17592186339930 1110 #uuid "d4bddb98-6829-5cd2-945b-a0864a4a8925" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339931 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi}{8}" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339931 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535253 true] [17592186339931 1111 #uuid "0c16d0e2-f600-56a4-a844-e0c981a38158" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339932 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi}{4}" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339932 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535253 true] [17592186339932 1111 #uuid "09aea622-558d-5eb6-aa78-4852385868b2" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339933 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339934 13194139535253 true] [17592186339933 1089 "q-352303" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339933 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535253 true] [17592186339933 1100 "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339933 1113 #uuid "1978d58f-4d27-5cb2-a88a-4942c49c5a7d" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339933 1145 "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}+\\frac{9}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))+\\frac{9}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{9}{8}(1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{8}+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi +18}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339934 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339935 13194139535253 true] [17592186339934 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535253 true] [17592186339934 1041 "field-1" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339934 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339935 13194139535253 true] [17592186339934 1110 #uuid "f28c30ed-7af0-5f7c-8b7e-585d920484af" 13194139535253 true] [17592186339935 1034 "\\frac{9\\pi}{8}+\\